From c51610af52bb011ca138a53a832b51f047b4f526 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 00:16:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Session status: a retained card with an explained
 wait is not a human ask; acknowledged exits leave failures

A chat stayed red (human_ask) for card t_2c750e700cdf6fae: a decision_retained
triage card with an open parent. Why: the stranded-park sweep wrote its generic
"decide this parked card" human_request because _excluded only honoured an
open parent for block_kind=dependency, not for a retained triage card. The
status reducer then read that request as a decision. Same card: `kanban
schedule` printed "Scheduled" with the card still triage, and a failed launch
process stayed in `failures` after `process_manage poll acknowledge=true`.

- kanban_retained_wait.explanation: a triage card whose latest run ended in
  decision_retained is explained by an open parent, or by an awaiting card
  (not closed) or clock recorded by a park after the retain.
- session outcome: such a card whose ask is the sweep's generated one
  (stranded_park_escalated newer than the retain) is a wait (`waiting_on`),
  not a decision. A request anyone else filed, a retained card with no parent
  or recorded wait, and a card with a done parent still show red.
- stranded-park sweep: no longer writes an ask on an explained retained card.
- canonical status: a failed process whose exit the agent consumed
  (poll acknowledge / wait / log) is dropped from work and from retained
  failures.
- `kanban schedule` reads the card back and exits non-zero with a clear error
  when the park was reported but the card did not reach scheduled.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_retained_wait_status.py (open parent
non-red; no parent/no wait red; done parent red; recorded card/clock non-red;
stale or closed waits red; real request red; sweep exclusion; schedule parks;
schedule that changes nothing errors) and test_session_status_refresh.py
(acknowledged failed process). Six of them fail on the previous code.
